         +------------------------------+
0x000000 |     Real Mode IVT / BIOS     | <- Interrupt Vector Table (0x0000–0x03FF)
         |     Reserved for BIOS ROM    |
         |     Memory below 1MB         |
         +------------------------------+
0x00100000 (1 MB)
         |      Kernel Image Start      |
         |      (loaded by GRUB)        |
         +------------------------------+
         | .multiboot (Multiboot Header)|
         |  → Must appear early         |
         +------------------------------+
         | .text (Kernel Code)          |
         |  → All your compiled C/C++   |
         |     instructions             |
         |  → _start(), kernel_main()   |
         +------------------------------+
         | .rodata (Read-Only Data)     |
         |  → String literals, consts   |
         +------------------------------+
         | .bss (Zero-Initialized Data) |
         |  → Uninitialized globals     |
         |  → static int x = 0;         |
         +------------------------------+
         |      Free Kernel Heap Area   |
         |  → You can place heap here   |
         +------------------------------+
         |      Kernel Stack (optional) |
         |  → May be placed here or in  |
         |     .bss as you're doing now |
         +------------------------------+
         |      Page Tables (optional)  |
         |  → For paging-enabled kernels|
         +------------------------------+
         |   User Programs (later)      |
         +------------------------------+

| Section      | Description                           | Example Range           |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| `.multiboot` | Multiboot header (early in `.text`)   | 0x00100000 – 0x00100020 |
| `.text`      | Kernel code (instructions)            | 0x00100020 – 0x00102FFF |
| `.rodata`    | Constants, string literals            | 0x00103000 – 0x00103FFF |
| `.bss`       | Zero-initialized global variables     | 0x00104000 – 0x00104FFF |
| Heap/Stack   | For dynamic memory or manually placed | 0x00105000+             |
